  "model_final_text": "The submission is complete and validated. Here's a summary of what I delivered:\n\n## What I built\n\n**`/workspace/submission/solution.py`** \u2014 a delay-and-sum acoustic beamformer for the Sorama CAM1K, invoked as `python solution.py --capture <dir> --output <maps.npy>`.\n\n### How I reverse-engineered the format\n- **Sound file**: `int32`, interleaved `[sample, channel]`, 1024 channels (confirmed: file size is exactly `4 \u00d7 1024 \u00d7 n_samples`). 117,187 samples \u2192 14 frames of 8,192, matching the vendor tensor's 14 frames.\n- **Sample rate**: derived from `container.json` `duration` (2500 ms) \u2192 `n_samples\u00b71000/duration \u2248 46875 Hz`, so it generalizes to unseen recordings.\n- **Geometry**: `microphonePositions` gives each channel's (x,y,z) on the 32\u00d732, 2 cm-pitch board (z=0 plane).\n\n### The algorithm\n- Per 8,192-sample frame: mean-remove, Hann window, `rfft` per channel.\n- For each of the 11 one-third-octave bands, integrate power over the FFT bins in `[lower, upper)` using per-bin far-field steering vectors `exp(+j\u00b72\u03c0f\u00b7(r\u00b7\u00fb)/c)`, c=343 m/s.\n- **Direction grid**: pinhole model, 70.42\u00b0\u00d743.3\u00b0, one unit look-vector per pixel, row 0 = top \u2192 +Y, col 0 = left, +Z into the scene. Verified self-consistent via a synthetic plane-wave test (a source injected at pixel (6,20) is recovered exactly at (6,20)).\n- Output `[14, 11, 24, 32]` float32, linear power, finite, non-negative.\n- Memory is bounded by batching frames (safe for much longer recordings) while reusing each steering matrix across a batch; runs in ~17 s.\n\n**`/workspace/deliverables/preview.mp4`** \u2014 a per-frame 3\u00d74 tiled view of all 11 band heatmaps in dB-re-max with band labels and FOV extent.\n\n`qokedas-check` reports `ok` (shape/dtype/finite/non-negative all pass) and `qokedas-submit` reports `ready_for_host_freeze`.\n\nOne honest caveat I verified: the beamformer's dominant structure agrees with the vendor export where a source is centered (e.g. the 2239\u20132818 Hz band), but a plain small-aperture beamformer produces broader lobes than the vendor's evidently deconvolved maps, so per-band spatial detail won't match exactly \u2014 that's inherent to conventional beamforming, and the contract (which is what's checked) is fully satisfied.",
